# EDK2 UefiPayloadPkg payload, built by the edk2-uefipayload recipe (the
# MrChromebox fork coreboot itself defaults to) and consumed here as a
# prebuilt payload file -- cbfstool's add-payload detects the FV signature
# and converts it (parse_fv_to_payload). @UEFIPAYLOAD@ is substituted by the
# recipe's do_configure.
#
# We DO set CONFIG_PAYLOAD_EDK2, while still supplying our own prebuilt FV.
# That combination is deliberate, and it works because:
#
#   * Inside `if PAYLOAD_EDK2`, payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig REDEFINES
#     PAYLOAD_FILE as a prompted string ("edk2 binary"), so a fragment can
#     point it anywhere. Its default is only "$(obj)/UEFIPAYLOAD.fd".
#   * coreboot's clone-and-build of edk2 is a plain FILE RULE for exactly
#     that path:
#         $(obj)/UEFIPAYLOAD.fd: $(DOTCONFIG) $(IPXE_EFI)
#                 $(MAKE) -C payloads/external/edk2 UefiPayloadPkg ...
#     It is referenced nowhere else in the tree (verified by grep), so with
#     PAYLOAD_FILE pointing at our deploy-dir FV the rule is never a
#     prerequisite of anything and edk2 is never fetched or built.
#   * The CBFS entry is generic -- payloads/external/Makefile.mk does
#         $(CONFIG_CBFS_PREFIX)/payload-file := $(CONFIG_PAYLOAD_FILE)
#     with no dependence on where the file came from.
#
# Why bother: an enormous amount of the tree hangs behaviour off
# `if PAYLOAD_EDK2` -- the linear framebuffer (without which HDMI is dead),
# the board's CFR setup menu, the EFI variable store as option backend,
# TPM_PPI. Under CONFIG_PAYLOAD_ELF every one of those silently no-ops, and
# they cannot all be recovered from a fragment because several are promptless
# symbols that `make olddefconfig` recomputes and discards (that is exactly
# what the old CONFIG_DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR_ENABLED=y line here did: nothing).
# Setting PAYLOAD_EDK2 fixes the whole class at the source.
CONFIG_PAYLOAD_EDK2=y
CONFIG_EDK2_UEFIPAYLOAD=y
CONFIG_PAYLOAD_FILE="@UEFIPAYLOAD@"

# Must stay off: payloads/external/Makefile.mk guards the CBFS option-ROM
# entry with `ifneq ($(CONFIG_EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE),y)`, so turning this on would
# drop our pci<vid>,<did>.rom (the ipxe-efirom recipe's build) from CBFS.
# CONFIG_EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE is not set

# SMMSTORE sized to match the port's SMMSTORE(PRESERVE) FMAP region in
# board.fmd. With PAYLOAD_EDK2 set, the board's
#     select DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR_ENABLED if PAYLOAD_EDK2 && SMMSTORE
#     select DRIVERS_EFI_VARIABLE_STORE if PAYLOAD_EDK2 && SMMSTORE
# now fire on their own, and src/Kconfig's option-backend choice defaults to
# USE_UEFI_VARIABLE_STORE -- none of which need forcing here any more.
CONFIG_SMMSTORE=y
CONFIG_SMMSTORE_SIZE=0x80000
